@startuml EngramModelSwitchUseCases
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam actorStyle awesome
skinparam usecase {
  BackgroundColor #f8fafc
  BorderColor #334155
  ArrowColor #334155
}
title Engram Vault - Use Case Diagram (Model Switching + Engram Continuity)

actor "Human User" as User
actor "MCP Agent Client" as Agent
actor "Project Admin" as Admin

rectangle "Engram Vault" {
  usecase "Authenticate and\\nOpen Workspace" as UC_AUTH
  usecase "Create Chat Session" as UC_CREATE
  usecase "Select Provider + Model\\n(OpenAI / Anthropic / Bedrock)" as UC_SELECT_MODEL
  usecase "Send Prompt" as UC_SEND
  usecase "Stream Assistant Response" as UC_STREAM
  usecase "Save Session as Engram" as UC_SAVE
  usecase "Derive Abstract Fallback\\nfrom Transcript" as UC_ABSTRACT
  usecase "Set Visibility Scope\\n(private / project)" as UC_VISIBILITY
  usecase "Tag and Keyword Memory" as UC_TAGS
  usecase "Pin Engram to Session" as UC_PIN
  usecase "Continue in New Chat" as UC_CONTINUE
  usecase "Switch Model for Follow-up\\nAnalysis" as UC_SWITCH_MODEL
  usecase "Query Project Engrams" as UC_QUERY
  usecase "Rehydrate Engram Context" as UC_REHYDRATE
  usecase "Generate Cross-Model\\nSynthesis" as UC_SYNTH
  usecase "Inspect Continuity Metadata\\n(used_engram_ids, source references)" as UC_METADATA
  usecase "Execute MCP Tool Calls\\n(JSON-RPC over SSE)" as UC_MCP
  usecase "Manage Access Scope\\nand Project Sharing Defaults" as UC_ACCESS
}

User --> UC_AUTH
User --> UC_CREATE
User --> UC_SEND
User --> UC_SAVE
User --> UC_PIN
User --> UC_CONTINUE
User --> UC_QUERY
User --> UC_REHYDRATE
User --> UC_SYNTH
User --> UC_METADATA

Admin --> UC_ACCESS
Admin --> UC_VISIBILITY

Agent --> UC_MCP

UC_CREATE .> UC_SELECT_MODEL : <<include>>
UC_SEND .> UC_STREAM : <<include>>

UC_SAVE .> UC_ABSTRACT : <<include>>
UC_SAVE .> UC_VISIBILITY : <<include>>
UC_SAVE .> UC_TAGS : <<include>>

UC_CONTINUE .> UC_SWITCH_MODEL : <<include>>
UC_CONTINUE .> UC_PIN : <<include>>

UC_SYNTH .> UC_QUERY : <<include>>
UC_SYNTH .> UC_REHYDRATE : <<include>>
UC_SYNTH .> UC_SEND : <<include>>

UC_METADATA .> UC_SYNTH : <<extend>>

UC_MCP .> UC_CREATE : <<include>>
UC_MCP .> UC_SEND : <<include>>
UC_MCP .> UC_SAVE : <<include>>
UC_MCP .> UC_QUERY : <<include>>
UC_MCP .> UC_REHYDRATE : <<include>>
UC_MCP .> UC_PIN : <<include>>

note right of UC_SWITCH_MODEL
Model switching pattern:
1) Save output as Engram E1
2) Continue to new session with different provider/model
3) Pin E1 and re-query supporting memory
4) Produce critique/synthesis
5) Save as Engram E2/E3
end note

note bottom of UC_METADATA
Validation target:
- response reflects prior memory
- used_engram_ids present when context reused
- source references available when citations are packed
end note

@enduml
